        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "f3d86ea4-8426-5578-b0c6-c003baaab4f0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Bands: Travis, Shiny Toy Guns\n- People: Fran Healy, Dougie Payne, Andy Dunlop, Neil Primrose, Harry Dean Stanton\n- Albums: The Man Who, We Are Pilots, Season of Poison, The Boy with No Name\n- Songs: Le Disko\n- Places: Glasgow, Los Angeles, California\n- Films: Paris, Texas\n- Awards: Grammy Award\n- Concepts: Alternative Songs Chart, media influence\n\nFacts:\n- Travis is a Scottish rock band formed in Glasgow in 1990 with members Fran Healy, Dougie Payne, Andy Dunlop, and Neil Primrose.\n- Travis took its name from the Harry Dean Stanton character Travis Henderson in the film Paris, Texas.\n- Travis's 1999 album The Man Who is widely credited by the media with helping pave the way for bands such as Keane and Coldplay to achieve worldwide success in the 2000s.\n- Shiny Toy Guns is an American rock band formed in Los Angeles, California, in 2002.\n- Shiny Toy Guns released its first studio album, We Are Pilots, in 2006 after recording it two previous times.\n- We Are Pilots by Shiny Toy Guns featured three singles that peaked inside the top 30 of the Alternative Songs Chart.\n- Le Disko is the first single by Shiny Toy Guns from the album We Are Pilots.\n- We Are Pilots by Shiny Toy Guns was nominated for a Grammy Award.\n- Shiny Toy Guns released its second album, Season of Poison, in 2008, and it featured two singles that peaked inside the top 30 of the Alternative Songs Chart.\n- The Boy with No Name is the fifth studio album by the Scottish indie pop band Travis.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "396e0eb6-6966-5a7a-af67-0b86dbc5d9a4",
        "text": "Page: Travis (band). Sentence: Travis is a Scottish rock band formed in Glasgow in 1990, composed of Fran Healy (lead vocals, rhythm guitar), Dougie Payne (bass guitar, backing vocals), Andy Dunlop (lead guitar, banjo, backing vocals) and Neil Primrose (drums, percussion).\nPage: Travis (band). Sentence: The band's name comes from the Harry Dean Stanton character Travis Henderson from the film \"Paris, Texas\".\nPage: Travis (band). Sentence: The band is widely claimed by the media as having paved the way for other bands such as Keane and Coldplay to go onto achieve worldwide success throughout the 2000s, particularly through the band's \"The Man Who\" (1999) album.\nPage: Shiny Toy Guns. Sentence: Shiny Toy Guns is an American rock band that formed in 2002 in Los Angeles, California.\nPage: Shiny Toy Guns. Sentence: They released their first studio album \"We Are Pilots\" in 2006, after recording it two previous times.\nPage: Shiny Toy Guns. Sentence: It featured three singles that peaked inside the top 30 in the Alternative Songs Chart.\nPage: Shiny Toy Guns. Sentence: \"We Are Pilots\" was nominated for a Grammy Award.\nPage: Shiny Toy Guns. Sentence: Their second album \"Season of Poison\" was released in 2008 and featured two singles that peaked inside the top 30 in the Alternative Songs Chart.\nPage: The Boy with No Name. Sentence: The Boy with No Name is the fifth studio album from Scottish indie pop band Travis.\nPage: Le Disko. Sentence: \"Le Disko\" is the first single by rock group Shiny Toy Guns from their album \"We Are Pilots\".",
